 comply with them. If you do not agree to these terms, you must not use our Website.</p><h2>There are other terms that may apply to you</h2>These terms of use refer to the following additional terms, which also apply to your use of our Website:<ul><li><h3><a href=\"/en/privacy-policy\">Our Privacy Policy</a></h3>This sets out how we handle your personal information and provides details about your rights in respect of the data we collect about you.</li><li><h3><a href=\"/en/cookie-settings\">Our Cookie Notice</a></h3>This is sets out information about the cookies we use on our Website.</li></ul><h2>Purpose of the Website</h2><p>The Website is the sheep and goat movement recording system for Wales.Our Website is directed at people living and farming in Wales. If you access the Website from outside Wales, the content may not be appropriate for you.</p><h2>We may make changes to the Website and these terms</h2><p>We regularly update our Website to improve the content and to reflect changes to our services. We may also update these terms from time to time, so please check back regularly.</p><h2>Authorised use of our Website and keeping your account details safe</h2><p>If you have been provided with specific log-in details, such as a username and password (or any other piece of information as part of our security procedures), you must keep this information safe. You must not disclose it to any third party. If we believe that you have not complied with these terms, we may disable your username and password at any time. If you know or suspect that anyone other than you knows your user identification or password, please contact us immediately.</p><h2>How we may use your personal information</h2><p>We will only use your personal information as set out in our Privacy Notice.</p><h2>Intellectual Property Rights</h2><p>You may not use any of our trade marks or trade names without our consent and you acknowledge that you have no ownership rights in and to any of those names and marks. You agree to notify us in writing promptly upon becoming aware of any unauthorised access to or use of the website by any party or of any claim that the website or any of the Content infringes any copyright, trade mark, or other contractual, statutory or common law rights of any party.</p><h2>We are not responsible for viruses and you must not introduce them</h2><p>We do not guarantee that our Website will be secure or free from bugs or viruses.You are responsible for configuring your IT, computer programmes and platform to access our Website. You should use your own virus protection software.</p><h2>Rules about linking to our Website</h2><p>You may link to our home page, provided you do so in a way that is fair and legal and does not damage our reputation or take advantage of it.</p><p>However, you must not under any circumstances:</p><ul><li>establish a link in such a way as to suggest any form of association, approval or endorsement on our part where none exists</li><li>establish a link to our Website in any website that is not owned by you</li><li>frame our Website on any other website, nor may you create a link to any part of our Website other than the home page</li></ul><p>If you wish to link to or make any use of content on our Website other than that set out above, please contact us.</p><h2>Website Accessibility</h2><p>We have tried to make the Website accessible to as many people as possible. please see our accessibility statement. If you have any comments about the accessibility of our Website, please email your suggestions to us.</p><h2>Which country’s laws apply to any disputes?</h2><p>These terms of use, their subject matter and their formation, are governed by the laws of England and Wales as applied in Wales. The courts of England and Wales sitting in Wales will have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any dispute or claim that arises out of or in connection with these terms.</p><hr/><h1>Terms and Conditions – BVDCymru</h1><h2>Please read these Terms and Conditions carefully before using this website</h2><p>These terms and conditions (“terms”) tell you the rules for using the BVDCymru Portal.</p><h2>Who we are and how to contact us?</h2><p>The BVDCymru Portal is operated by EIDCymru (&quot;we&quot; or &quot;us&quot;).To contact us, please email <a href=\"mailto:bvd@eidcymru.org\">bvd@eidcymru.org</a> or write to us at: BVDCymru, Tŷ Merlin, Parc Merlin, Aberystwyth, SY23 3FF.</p><h2>By using the BVDCymru Portal you accept these terms</h2><p>By using the BVDCymru Portal you confirm that you accept these terms and that you agree to comply with them. If you do not agree to these terms, you must not use the BVDCymru Portal.</p><h2>There are other terms that may apply to you</h2><p>These terms refer to <a href=\"/en/privacy-policy\">Our Privacy Policy</a>, which also applies to your use of the BVDCymru Portal.</p><p>This policy sets out how we handle your personal information and provides details about your rights in respect of the data we collect about you.</p><p><a href=\"/en/cookie-settings\">Our Cookie Notice</a> sets out how we handle your personal information and provides details about your rights in respect of the data we collect about you.</p><h2>Purpose of the BVDCymru Portal</h2><p>The BVDCymru Portal’s primary purpose is to support the Bovine Viral Diarrhoea (Wales) Order 2024.</p><h2>We may make changes to the BVDCymru Portal and these terms</h2><p>We regularly update the BVDCymru Portal to improve the content and to reflect changes to our services. We may also update these terms from time to time, so please check back regularly. Any changes made shall be binding on you, and by continuing to use the BVDCymru Portal you agree to accept those changes.</p><h2>Authorised use of the BVDCymru Portal and keeping your account details safe</h2><p>If you have been provided with specific log-in details, such as a username and password (or any other piece of information as part of our security procedures), you must keep this information safe. You must not disclose it to any third party. If we believe that you have not complied with these terms, we may disable your username and password at any time.  If you know or suspect that anyone other than you knows your user identification or password, please contact us immediately.</p><p>You agree that you will not use the the BVDCymru Portal Site for any purpose that is unlawful or prohibited by these terms.</p><h2>How we may use your personal information</h2><p>We will only use your personal information as set out in<!-- --> <a href=\"/en/privacy-policy\">Our Privacy Policy</a></p><h2>Intellectual Property Rights</h2><p>We are the owner or the licensee of all intellectual property rights in the BVDCymru Portal, and in the material published on it (including the design and all logos, text and graphics). Those works are protected by copyright and other intellectual property rights.</p><p>You may not use any of our materials, logos, trade marks, services, products or names without our consent and you acknowledge that you have no ownership rights in and to any of those materials or marks. You agree to notify us in writing promptly upon becoming aware of any unauthorised use of the intellectual property rights in the BVDCymru Portal by any party or of any claim that the BVDCymru Portal or any of its content infringes any copyright, trade mark, or other contractual, statutory or common law rights of any party.</p><h2>We are not responsible for viruses and you must not introduce them</h2><p>We do not guarantee that the BVDCymru Portal will be secure or free from bugs or viruses.  You are responsible for configuring your IT, computer programmes and platform to access the BVDCymru Portal. You should use your own virus protection software.</p><h2>Our responsibility for loss or damage suffered by you</h2><p>To the fullest extent allowed by law, we exclude all conditions, warranties, representations or other terms which may apply to the BVDCymru Portal.</p><p>We do not promise that the BVDCymru Portal will meet your needs or expectations or that your use of the BVDCymru Portal will be uninterrupted, secure, virus or error free.</p><p>We will not be liable to you for any loss or damage arising from or in connection with:</p><ul><li>your use of, or inability to use, the BVDCymru Portal;</li><li>your use of or reliance on any content displayed on the BVDCymru Portal;</li><li>any errors, omissions, interruptions, delays, bugs or viruses on the BVDCymru Portal; and</li><li>any decision by us to turn off or remove any content, services or external links.</li></ul><p>In particular, we will not be liable to you for any loss of profit, loss of business, business interruption, loss of business opportunity, or any indirect or consequential loss or damage connected with your use of the BVDCymru Portal.</p><p>We do not exclude or limit in any way our liability to you where it would be unlawful to do so. This includes liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence or the negligence of our employees, agents or subcontractors and for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation.</p><p>If defective digital content that we have supplied damages a device or digital content belonging to you and this is caused by our failure to use reasonable care and skill, you might be able to ask for compensation under consumer protection law, although this isn’t guaranteed.</p><h2>Rules about linking to the BVDCymru Portal</h2><p>You may link to our home page, provided you do so in a way that is fair and legal and does not damage our reputation or take advantage of it.</p><p>However, you must not under any circumstances:</p><ul><li>establish a link in such a way as to suggest any form of association, approval or endorsement on our part where none exists;</li><li>establish a link to the BVDCymru Portal in any website that is not owned by you; or</li><li>frame the BVDCymru Portal on any other website, nor may you create a link to any part of the BVDCymru Portal other than the home page.</li></ul><p>If you wish to link to or make any use of content on the BVDCymru Portal other than that set out above, please contact us.</p><p>We may withdraw our permission to link to the BVDCymru Portal at any time.</p><h2>BVDCymru Portal Accessibility</h2><p>We have tried to make the BVDCymru Portal accessible to as many people as possible. Please see<!-- --> <a href=\"/en/accessibility\">our accessibility statement</a>. If you have any comments about the accessibility of the BVDCymru Portal, please email your suggestions to us.</p><h2>Which country’s laws apply to any disputes?</h2><p>These terms, their subject matter and their formation, are governed by the laws of England and Wales as applied in Wales.  The courts of England and Wales sitting in Wales will have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any dispute or claim that arises out of or in connection with these terms.</p></div></div></div>','Terms and Conditions','','inherit','closed','closed','','8-revision-v1','','','2026-01-05 14:50:45','2026-01-05 14:50:45','',8,'http://localhost:8081/?p=21',0,'revision','',0),(22,0,'2026-01-05 14:50:46','2026-01-05 14:50:46','<div style=\"padding:28px\"><div style=\"max-width:1024px;margin:0 auto\"><div class=\"BodyStyling_bodyStyling__ZUhcU\"><h1>Accessibility statement for EIDCymru and BVDCymru</h1><p>This website is funded by the Welsh Government and the accessibility statement applies to the entire EIDCymru website. The website is built and run by EIDCymru developers.</p><h2>How you should be able to use this website</h2><p>We want as many people as possible to be able to use this website. You should be able to:</p><ul><li>change colours, contrast levels and fonts using assistive technology</li><li>zoom in up to 300% without the text spilling off the screen</li><li>navigate most of the website using just a keyboard</li><li>navigate most of the website using speech recognition software</li><li>use most of the website using a screen reader (including the most recent versions of JAWS, NVDA and VoiceOver)</li></ul><p>We&#x27;ve also made the website text as simple as possible to understand.</p><p>AbilityNet has advice on<!-- --> <a href=\"https://mcmw.abilitynet.org.uk/\" target=\"_blank\">making your device easier to use</a> <!-- -->if you have a disability.</p><h2>How accessible this website is</h2><p>We know some parts of this website are not fully accessible:</p><ul><li>You can&#x27;t modify the line height or spacing of text.</li><li>The text won&#x27;t reflow in a single column when you change the size of the browser window.</li><li>Some of our online forms are difficult to navigate using just a keyboard.</li><li>You can&#x27;t skip to the main content when using a screen reader.</li><li>Programmatic language of the page is sometimes set to English when the language selected is Welsh.</li><li>Navigating using speech recognition speech recognition software (such as Dragon by Nuance) includes inefficient workarounds such as using unlabelled dictation or indirect mouse emulation, which are not reliable or inclusive.</li></ul><h2>Feedback and contact information</h2><p>If you need information on this website in a different format like accessible PDF, large print, easy read, audio recording or braille, please contact us via the following channels:</p><ul><li>Email: <a href=\"mailto:contact@eidcymru.org\">contact@eidcymru.org</a>.</li><li>Call us on:<!-- --> <a aria-label=\"Contact EIDCymru by phone\" href=\"tel:01970636959\">01970 636 959</a>.</li></ul><p>Some of the website information is readily available in alternate formats.</p><p>To help us better meet your needs, please tell us the alternate format you would like to receive, and if you use any assistive technologies.</p><p>We&#x27;ll consider your request and get back to you in 10 working days.</p><h2>Reporting accessibility problems with this website</h2><p>If you find any problems that are not listed on this page or you think we&#x27;re not meeting the accessibility requirements, please contact us.</p><h2>Enforcement procedure</h2><p>The Equality and Human Rights Commission (EHRC) is responsible for enforcing the Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2) Accessibility Regulations 2018 (the &#x27;accessibility regulations&#x27;).</p><p>If you’re not happy with how we respond to your complaint,<!-- --> <a href=\"https://www.equalityadvisoryservice.com/\" target=\"_blank\">contact the Equality Advisory and Support Service (EASS)</a>.</p><h2>Contacting us by phone</h2><p>Currently we are not providing a text relay service, audio induction loops, or British Sign Language (BSL) interpreter. However, we are looking into the feasibility of providing these services.</p><p>Call us on 01970 636 959 if you have any accessibility related questions.</p><h2>Technical information about this website&#x27;s accessibility</h2><p>EIDCymru is committed to making its website accessible, in accordance with the Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2) Accessibility Regulations 2018.</p><h2>Compliance status</h2><p>This website is partially compliant with the<!-- --> <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/\" target=\"_blank\">Web Content Accessibility Guidelines version 2.2</a> <!-- -->AA standard. Non-accessible success criterion are listed below.</p><h2>Non-accessible success criterion</h2><p>The content listed below is non-accessible for the following reasons:</p><ul><li>1.1.1 Non-text Content (Level A)<br/>Some documents may be in non- HTML formats, for example PDF. These may not be fully accessible due to missing text alternatives and missing document structure. However, accessible formats are provided on request to ensure users have a suitable alternative when required.</li><li>2.4.1 Bypass Blocks (Level A)<br/>On certain pages the skip to main content links do not directly lead to the main content</li><li>2.4.11 Focus Not Obscured (Level AA)<br/>Some elements on the page are not highlighted when focus is moved onto them</li><li>2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum) (Level AA)<br/>Some targets on the page do not meet a minimum size of 24px and have insufficient spacing around them</li><li>3.1.1 Language of Page (Level A)<br/>Programmatic language of the page is set to English when the language selected is Welsh.</li><li>4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (Level A)<br/>Navigating using speech recognition speech recognition software (such as Dragon by Nuance) includes inefficient workarounds such as using unlabelled dictation or indirect mouse emulation, which are not reliable or inclusive.</li></ul><h2>Known issues with workarounds</h2><h3>Inventory speech dictation</h3><p><a href=\"https://eidcymru.org/app/inventory#page5\" target=\"_blank\">https://eidcymru.org/app/inventory#page5</a><br/>Page Title: Step 5 of 5 - Gathering Dates (Optional step and can be skipped)</p><ul><li>When navigating using dictation software to the enter start date and end date, the “from” and “to” labels are not present, resulting in the form fields being un-selectable.</li><li>You can dictate keyboard navigation commands to navigate the form as a workaround.</li></ul><h3>Clipping and Shearing date selection</h3><ul><li>Dictate “Click Clipping and Shearing Start Date” to select the first box.</li><li>Dictate “Click Clipping and Shearing End Date” to select the second box.</li></ul><h3>Dipping date selection</h3><ul><li>Dictate “Dipping Start Date” to select the first box.</li><li>Dictate “Dipping End Date” to select the second box.</li></ul><h3>Lambing date selection</h3><ul><li>Dictate “Lambing Start Date” to select the first box.</li><li>Dictate “Lambing End Date” to select the second box.</li></ul><h3>BVDCymru logo lacking alternative text</h3><ul><li>The logo image is an SVG element so a title attribute is sufficient for screen readers.</li></ul><h3>The &quot;Rows per page&quot; dropdown input is missing a form label:</h3><ul><li>An aria-labelled by is present and the label is read when the element is tabbed to using a screen reader.</li></ul><h2>Known issues currently being addressed</h2><h3>BVDCymru logo link has unclear purpose for screen readers</h3><ul><li>The BVD Cymru logo link has a title and aria-label of ‘back to dashboard’ which only makes sense when the user is logged into the BVD service.</li></ul><h3>BVDCymru Account Management pages contains proprietary code with accessibility issues</h3><p>Our developers don&#x27;t have access to the code on the account management pages. The following issues have been logged as outside of our control:</p><ul><li>&#x27;General&#x27; heading needs to be an &lt;h2&gt;.</li><li>&#x27;Select a locale&#x27; needs to be correctly associated with a form control.</li><li>All buttons need to be given a value attribute.</li><li>ARIA attributes need to point to a valid, existing id or be removed if it&#x27;s unnecessary.</li><li>Cancel button needs appropriate functionality and behaviour.</li></ul><h3>The drag and drop input is missing a form label</h3><ul><li>&#x27;Delete&#x27; text added to the bin icon to make actions clearer.</li><li>We acknowledge this is an issue and are currently in the process of redesigning the form page accordingly.</li></ul><h3>Global Issue with language toggler</h3><ul><li>Users will have difficulty using the language toggler with speech dictation software.</li><li>We acknowledge this is a global issue and are in the process of changing the labels and design to improve accessibility.</li></ul><h2>Disproportionate burden</h2><p>EIDCymru recognises that achieving full accessibility may sometimes impose a disproportionate burden due to financial, technical, or logistical constraints. While striving to meet accessibility standards, any claims of disproportionate burden will be thoroughly evaluated, documented, and addressed through reasonable alternatives to minimise barriers wherever feasible.</p><h2>Content that&#x27;s not within the scope of the accessibility regulations</h2><p>The accessibility regulations do not require us to fix PDFs or other documents published before 23 September 2018 if they&#x27;re not essential to providing our services. We will endeavour to ensure any new PDFs or documents we publish will meet the accessibility standards and best practice.</p><h2>What we are doing to improve accessibility</h2><p>We are currently working on the new version of EIDCymru.</p><p>Redevelopment plans for the new EIDCymru version include:</p><ul><li>Correct content that meets the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 AA standard.</li><li>The website working on the most commonly used assistive technologies - including screen magnifiers, screen readers, speech recognition and dictation tools.</li><li>User research that includes users of assistive technologies.</li><li>Manual testing with people who have a range of disabilities on desktop, mobile, and tablet devices using the Digital Accessibility Centre (DAC).</li></ul><h2>Preparation of this accessibility statement</h2><p>This statement was prepared on 29th November 2024. It was last reviewed on 4th December 2024.</p><p>This website was last tested in November 2024 against the WCAG 2.2 AA standard. The test was carried out by Welsh Government and EIDCymru developers and testers.</p><p>A combination of methods is advised by the UK Government Digital Service. Automated, semi-automated and manual checks have been conducted on our main website platform.</p><p>The site has been tested using the following tools:</p><ul><li>WAVE Chrome browser extension.</li><li>Axe® Accessibility online system.</li><li>Dragon by Nuance.</li><li>ZoomText.</li><li>Screen Readers: ChromeVOX (Chrome Screen Reader), Windows Text-To-Speech, Apple Spoken Content.</li><li>Colour Contrast Analyser (CCA).</li><li>AChecker.</li></ul><p>Critical issues that were found by these tools were catalogued and fixed by the EIDCymru development team.</p></div></div></div>','Accessibility','','inherit','closed','closed','','10-revision-v1','','','2026-01-05 14:50:46','2026-01-05 14:50:46','',10,'http://localhost:8081/?p=22',0,'revision','',0),(23,0,'2026-01-05 14:50:48','2026-01-05 14:50:48','<div class=\"CookieSettings_background__7SpDk\"><div class=\"CookieSettings_container__m8UNE\"><div class=\"Panel-module_panel__nwNeT Panel-module_info__w6QiA Panel-module_base__QITrV CookieSettings_infoPanel__nGbff\"><div class=\"Panel-module_text__7mibq\"><span class=\"CookieSettings_h2__9x__r\">Your cookie settings have not yet been stored</span><span>EIDCymru.org places cookies when you visit our website. You can adjust these settings according to your preferences. Please remember to save this page with your updated choices.</span></div></div><div class=\"CookieSettings_body__x5KZ6\"><h1>Cookie Settings</h1><p>Cookies are small files saved on your phone, tablet, or computer when you visit a website. We use them to monitor your activity on the EIDCymru.org site, such as the pages you view. These cookies do not collect any personal information about you.</p><div class=\"CookieSettings_expandable__uCDzz\"><div class=\"CookieSettings_title__w9coz\"><svg width=\"8\" height=\"10\" viewBox=\"0 0 8 10\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M7.5 4.13397C8.16667 4.51887 8.16667 5.48113 7.5 5.86603L1.5 9.33013C0.833334 9.71503 1.22038e-07 9.2339 1.12858e-07 8.4641L3.02403e-08 1.5359C2.10605e-08 0.766098 0.833333 0.284973 1.5 0.669873L7.5 4.13397Z\" fill=\"#004268\"></path></svg><button>Read more about our cookie policy</button></div></div><p>We utilise three types of cookies (cookies that measure website use, cookies that help with communication and marketing, and strictly necessary cookies), and you can change the following:</p><button class=\"Button-module_primary__st6yY Button-module_base__f8MM- Button-module_sm__RXFPY Button-module_rightIcon__JtN3M CookieSettings_saveButton__E01bM\" data-testid=\"save-changes\"><span class=\"Button-module_content__PpY